Description: pco: skip default sample check and alpha-to-coverage when static
 Every non-internal fragment shader gets a default sample check
 (sample_mask_in & (1 << sample_id), discard when zero) and the
 alpha-to-coverage lowering, both driven by the FS meta word. With a
 static single sample count the default check equals the helper
 invocation test, which already uses sample_mask_in including the sample
 mask from the meta word. With alpha-to-coverage statically disabled the
 lowering only adds dead code. Record both static states in pco_fs_data
 and skip the passes then. Explicit gl_SampleMask writes keep their check.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
